  "aiContextParagraph": "Discussions regarding a potential successor to the Indonesian Vice Presidency have intensified, with several political groups aligning behind Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, who currently serves as Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives. Recent endorsements originate from both labor organizations, such as the KSPSI, and various regional chapters of the Gerindra Party, including those in Jakarta, Bali, and Gorontalo. Supporters frequently emphasize his legislative experience and ability to maintain political stability as primary reasons for his suitability. Additionally, the NasDem Party has publicly indicated that his presence could assist the President in governance. Reports suggest a broader consensus among political party chairs that the vacancy should be filled by a representative from the Gerindra Party, with other internal candidates also being mentioned in current discourse surrounding the vice presidential selection process.",
